    "q": "How does pretibial myxedema differ from myxedema?",
    "a": "Pretibial myxedema (Graves) = mucopolysaccharide deposition in skin plus surrounding edema, and is only seen in Graves. Myxedema means severe hypothyroidism in general, not just skin changes, and can cause carpal tunnel syndrome. Pretibial myxedema in Hashimoto is astronomically rare.",
